    {
      "short": "Stuffing",
      "chapter": "problem",
      "title": "Someone else's leak",
      "body": [
        "Nestegg's hashing is solid. It doesn't matter. Bots take billions of email/password pairs leaked from <i>other</i> sites and try them here: <span class=\"term\">credential stuffing</span>.",
        "About 2% of attempts succeed, because people reuse passwords. Each success looks like a perfectly normal login. Rate limits per IP, bot detection and rejecting known-breached passwords all help — but as long as a password alone is enough, some will get in."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Bots replaying leaked passwords",
        "~ 2% of attempts take over an account"
      ],
      "metrics": {
        "leak": "weak ones, slowly",
        "stuffing": 2,
        "mfa": "no"
      },
      "scene": {
        "entities": {
          "users": {
