    {
      "short": "Passkeys",
      "chapter": "solution",
      "title": "No shared secret at all",
      "body": [
        "<span class=\"term\">Passkeys</span> (WebAuthn) replace the password with a key pair. The private key never leaves the user's device and is unlocked by fingerprint or PIN; Nestegg stores only the public key.",
        "To sign in, the device signs a fresh challenge — and the signature is bound to <code>nestegg.app</code>, so a look-alike phishing site gets nothing usable. A leaked database contains only public keys, and there's no password to stuff."
      ],
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Roll passkeys out alongside passwords + MFA, then nudge users over. Keep a safe recovery path — it's now the weakest link."
      },
      "changes": [
