    {
      "short": "OIDC",
      "chapter": "technique",
      "title": "Let someone else check",
      "body": [
        "Nestegg's business app lets employees of client companies log in with their work account. With <span class=\"term\">OAuth 2.0</span> plus <span class=\"term\">OpenID Connect</span>, the user is sent to their company's <b>identity provider</b>, signs in there (with its own MFA), and comes back with a one-time code.",
        "Nestegg's server swaps the code for a signed <b>ID token</b> naming the user. Nestegg never sees a password. OAuth alone is about <i>delegated access</i> (\"this app may read my calendar\"); OIDC adds the identity layer on top."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ Sign in with the company identity provider",
        "- Passwords for business accounts"
      ],
